              "text": "چاند (chā̃d) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from candra, \"moon\" (CDIAL 4661). CDIAL lists it under the noun candra, \"moon\", built on the adjective candra, \"shining\"."
